choice("Continue", B3-Ch12b-Allout2, v_current_scene = B3-Ch12b-Allout2)


ID: B3-Ch12b-Allout2
TEXT:

I drop like a stone, hitting the turf beside an uprooted pine trunk untouched by the flames. I hoist the multi-ton log with both hands, channeling maxed Strength and Speed, and charge Eiden in a sonic blur.

The pine trunk crashes into his flank with the force of a battering ram, catching him completely off-guard. The impact hurls him through four standing trees before he displaces in a flash of light, reappearing ten paces out with dust clinging to his tunic.

"I must admit, Barry," Eiden murmurs, his smile flattening, "that was mildly annoying."

I swing the log in a crushing downward arc to squash him into the dirt, but the wood smashes empty cobblestone as Eiden vanishes.

"Behind you!" Arraka roars. "Invisible!"

Without breaking stride, I spin on my heel, whirling the entire trunk around me in a vicious horizontal circle. The wood smashes into his cloaked form, breaking the invisibility weave and pitching him backward twenty paces. Eiden recovers mid-air, teleports directly in front of me, and grabs the log with one bare hand, shattering the wood into thousands of splinters.

Weaponless, I sprint toward another fallen trunk, wrench it from the dirt, and heave it through the air like a javelin. As Eiden detonates the flying timber with a fire lance, I scoop up jagged boulders and pelt them in rapid succession.

Hadrik catches the rhythm, uprooting a massive pine of his own and leaping from above to hammer Eiden's skull.

"This is becoming absurd," Eiden mutters, catching Hadrik's trunk with his left palm while deflecting my stone barrage with his right.

Eiden teleports beside me, hand glowing with a targeted incantation. I push my superhuman speed and reflexes to the redline, weaving left and right in jagged zigzag bursts faster than the eye can follow, denying him any clean lock.

Frustrated, Eiden manifests ten massive boulders in mid-air and launches the entire spread at once. I halt for a fraction of a second to punch clean through the central rock, but the hesitation gives him the window to engulf me in a roaring blast of fire. Heat blisters against my skin, but my maxed Aura Hardening absorbs the thermal shockwave, keeping my flesh intact.

Daren's enchanted sword streaks in from the flank, spinning like a scythe and forcing Eiden onto the defensive as he repeatedly teleports to escape the homing edge.

The window is closing. If Eiden tires of this and shifts into his true combat form, no weapon in the world can save us.

"Illuna, dish-washing spell!" I yell over the roar of wind. "He is too scattered to hold his ward balance!"

"Attempting it," Illuna calls down. "No promises."

Illuna focuses, snapping a dense sphere of swirling water directly over Eiden's head as he evades Daren's blade. The sudden immersion catches him mid-breath; he thrashes in mid-air, coughing and gasping as he struggles to dodge the whistling sword.

Unable to break the water lock or shake the blade, Eiden conjures a localized vortex around his own body. The roaring winds tear Illuna's water sphere into mist, while the spinning blade is swept into the gale, forcing Daren to recall his weapon.

Eiden collapses the whirlwind and drops to one knee on the highway, clutching his forehead with one hand, his balance shattered. His equilibrium is reeling.

The opening is here.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch12b-Blinding, v_current_scene = B3-Ch12b-Blinding)


ID: B3-Ch12b-Together
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch11_red == 0 && v_b3_ch12_scout == 0) {
