"A fifth?" Hadrik roars. "You arrogant little—"

A wave of flame washes across the cobblestone. Daren locks his shield in front of Hadrik, while Illuna drops a roaring pillar of water to shield our climb.

}
#if(v_b3_ch12_scout != 0) {
"Move," I tell Illuna.

Flower launches into the air, twin fire jets blasting from her boots, while I channel my air currents to lift off behind her.

Ahead of us, Daren and Hadrik have turned the highway into a disaster zone. Half the pines along the verge lie splintered or shorn by Daren's floating steel, and Eiden drifts through the wreckage with effortless grace, barely tapping his deeper reserves.

When Flower draws near, Illuna conjures three water lances and hurls them downward. Eiden raises his right palm, flash-boiling the projectiles into steam with a torrent of white flame.

"More guests?" Eiden smiles, raising an eyebrow. "Shall we move to a fifth, then?"

"A fifth?" Hadrik roars. "You arrogant little—"

A wave of flame washes across the cobblestone. Daren locks his shield in front of Hadrik, while Illuna drops a roaring pillar of water to shield our climb.

}
"We press him together," I shout to Illuna and Flower. "I'll draw his attention with projectile spells."

"Testing your newly minted sorcery on a stillwater, Barry?" Eiden's voice floats up as he materializes ten feet from my flank. "By all means, let us see the fruits of your labor."

I kick my air currents backward to gain breathing room, opening with a basic lightning dart to probe his ward geometry.

"The standard western opener," Eiden remarks, drifting lazily through the air. "Did you find an exploit in my passive shielding?"

He is baiting me. The lightning arc revealed a glaring gap in his ward alignment that even a novice would spot. But against my single point in magic, he wouldn't bother arming a rebound trap. I play his game.

I condense three small icicles and launch them simultaneously along separate converging vectors. They slip clean through the intentional gap in his barrier, one of the frost needles slicing across his right shoulder, drawing a thin line of crimson.

"Fascinating," Eiden purrs, passing his left palm over the cut to seal the skin instantly. "Few mortals draw blood from a stillwater. Was it worth a lifetime of striving for this singular triumph?"

"I am trembling with joy," I say flatly.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch12b-Together2, v_current_scene = B3-Ch12b-Together2)


ID: B3-Ch12b-Together2
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b3_ch10_eiden == 0 && v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b3_ch11_transferred == 0 && v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 1 || v_b3_ch11_transferred == 1 && v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 1 || v_b3_ch11_transferred == 0 && v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_b3_ch10_eiden != 0 || v_b3_ch11_transferred == 1 && v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_b3_ch10_eiden != 0)
#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0) {
"Shall we raise the stakes?" Eiden smiles, snapping his fingers as a dozen localized detonations ignite across my flight path.

I recognize the incantation. Dodging concussive blasts in mid-air is exhausting, but the baseline matrix runs for fifteen seconds. If I maintain my evasive roll, the sequence will expire.

I spend fifteen agonizing seconds banking and diving through the shockwaves. When the counter reaches zero, I ease my drift, anticipating the lull.

The blasts do not stop. Instead, the frequency doubles, the detonations closing in like a tightening net.

}
#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 1) {
"Where is your form, Hadrik?" Daren calls up from the highway. "You moved twice as fast this morning! Are you drunk again?"

"Quiet!" Hadrik snarls. "Sparring you is easy—I know your habits. But while I'm sober, there's a trick I've been meaning to try."

A pair of massive eagle wings erupts from Hadrik's shoulder blades, the feathers rippling with transmutation magic like Gontrok's hybrid forms in Ollendor. With a single thundering downstroke, he rockets into the sky, crossing the gap in a heartbeat to hammer a brutal fist into Eiden's jaw.

"Hah!" Hadrik hovers on beating wings, grinning ear to ear. "I knew the wings would handle cleaner without ale in my gut! Almost makes me want to stay sober. Almost!"

He dives into a savage exchange, forcing Eiden to trade blows in mid-air as they streak across the treeline.

Hadrik is buying us time, but I need to seize the initiative before Eiden adjusts his rhythm.

}
#if(v_b3_ch10_eiden == 0 && v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0) {
The spell matrix should have expired. The daily limit is absolute. Did I misread the incantation?

I twist frantically through the air, but the explosions multiply until the sky fills with fire and concussive thunder. Three direct blasts strike my chest, tearing through my aura and ending my life in an instant.

}
#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_b3_ch10_eiden != 0) {
Arraka's lecture from two days ago flashes through my mind. During the Still Winter, Eiden abused a structural flaw in this exact matrix to stretch its duration indefinitely, just as he exploited the time-freeze loop. But sustaining the weave introduces an inverse vulnerability.

Movement feeds the chain.

I cut my currents instantly, hanging motionless in the sky.

Without kinetic displacement to sustain the loop, the detonation runes fizzle out, vanishing into the breeze.

"Arraka's counsel holds," I call out to Eiden, who floats twenty paces away. "Still using the same loop exploits from six centuries ago."

"Ah," Eiden murmurs. "Arraka again."

Defending is a losing proposition. I must force the offensive.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b3_ch10_eiden == 0 && v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0)
