ID: B3-Ch12b-Orangutan
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_bluff == 4 || v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_bluff < 4 || v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 1 && v_bluff < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 1 && v_bluff == 4)
#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_bluff < 4) {
"Eiden, behind you!" I shout. "Azarius just dropped his concealment!"

"Azarius?" Eiden asks, drifting in mid-air with his eyes closed. "The grand magister is far too fond of dramatic entrances to strike from the shadows unannounced. A rather crude deception, wouldn't you say?"

"Aren't you going to check?" I ask.

"Hardly," Eiden replies. "And playing the grand magister's name as a cheap distraction is an insult to both of us. Allow me to demonstrate a proper greeting."

}
#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 1 && v_bluff < 4) {
"Eiden, behind you!" I shout. "Azarius just dropped his concealment!"

"Azarius?" Eiden parries Hadrik's fist without looking. "The grand magister is far too fond of dramatic entrances to strike from the shadows unannounced. A rather crude deception, wouldn't you say?"

"Aren't you going to check?" I ask.

"Hardly," Eiden replies. "And playing the grand magister's name as a cheap distraction is an insult to both of us. Allow me to demonstrate a proper greeting."

}
#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_bluff == 4) {
"Eiden, behind you!" I shout. "Azarius just dropped his concealment!"

"What?" Eiden actually glances over his shoulder, scanning the empty sky behind him. "Ah... I see. You leveled your Bluff stat. The inflection was remarkably convincing. But what was the objective? Shouldn't you have attacked while my back was turned?"

"In hindsight, yes, that would have been smarter," I admit.

"Well, not a total loss," Eiden smiles. "Though invoking Azarius to buy three seconds of life is a gamble that carries a price. Allow me to collect it."

}
#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 1 && v_bluff == 4) {
"Eiden, behind you!" I shout. "Azarius just dropped his concealment!"

"What?" Eiden turns his head for a single heartbeat, checking the sky behind him.

One second is all Hadrik needs. He brings both clenched fists down like an anvil onto the crown of Eiden's skull, driving the stillwater straight into the cobblestones and leaving a smoking crater where he impacts.

As Eiden pushes himself from the rubble, Illuna snaps a dense sphere of water over his head. The sudden submersion catches him mid-breath; he thrashes in the dirt, choking against the fluid seal. He tries flying sideways to break the tether, but Illuna's morning drills pay off, keeping the water sphere locked to his neck.

Kate raises her scepter from the roadside, mana gathering in the gem.

"Kate, hold!" I shout, and she lowers the staff on command.

He is dazed, but far from helpless. If Kate channels now, his passive wards can still deflect the beam. We need one final disruption to shatter his balance.

Daren hurls his sword into a whistling spin toward Eiden's chest. Eiden wrenches a jagged stone spire from the pavement to deflect the steel, then conjures a roaring whirlwind around his own body. The centrifugal gale tears Illuna's water sphere into spray and scatters the moisture across the grass.

Eiden dismisses the vortex and drops to one knee on the broken road, pressing a hand against his temples. His equilibrium is completely scrambled.

Now.

}
#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 || v_bluff < 4) {
A localized pressure wave detonates directly in front of my chest, ripping the air from my lungs. Before I can raise an aura ward or bank away on the currents, Eiden's compressed gravity lance snaps through the center of my ribcage, obliterating flesh and bone in a single concussive rupture.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_bluff == 4 || v_bluff < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_bluff == 4 || v_bluff < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0 && v_bluff == 4 || v_bluff < 4)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch12b-Blinding, v_current_scene = B3-Ch12b-Blinding) if (v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 1 && v_bluff == 4)


ID: B3-Ch12b-Dagger
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 0) {
"Time to draw the trump card," I say, flashing a confident grin.

"A trump card?" Eiden tilts his head. "Color me intrigued. Let us see it."

I draw my steel dagger from its sheath, holding the point steady toward his chest.

Eiden stares at the six-inch blade in silence. "You cannot be serious."

}
#if(v_b3_ch12_hadrik == 1) {
"Hadrik, clear the line!" I yell. "I've got this!"

"If you say so," Hadrik banks wide on his eagle wings, giving us space. "Don't get yourself killed!"

"I admire the bravado, Barry," Eiden says, drifting closer. "Have you finally devised a master stroke?"

"Watch and learn," I say, drawing my steel dagger and leveling the point at his throat.

Eiden stares at the six-inch blade in silence. "You cannot be serious."

}
"Did I ever recount how I took down Arraka in her primordial form with nothing but a steel blade?" I ask, stepping forward on my air currents.

"Your aura indicates you aren't lying," Eiden muses, "though I suspect critical context has been aggressively omitted."

"Draw your own conclusions," I say. "Here I come!"

I rocket toward Eiden, slashing in sharp diagonals. He sways and glides around every thrust with effortless economy, his closed eyes radiating mild bewilderment. After half a dozen empty swings whistle through thin air, the brilliance of my plan looks significantly dimmer.

"Is this the extent of the spectacle, Barry?" Eiden asks as I pull back to catch my breath. "Winded already? The legendary dagger has barely shown its pedigree. Allow me to offer an attack worthy of such an artifact."

White flame ignites along his outstretched palm, condensing into a searing thermal beam aimed dead center at my chest. If that heat connects, no baseline ward can hold the line.

choice("Fly straight at Eiden while he's overconfident and stab him with my dagger.", B3-Ch12b-Overconfident, v_current_scene = B3-Ch12b-Overconfident)
choice("Fly away from Eiden and try to think of a different plan.", B3-Ch12b-Away, v_current_scene = B3-Ch12b-Away)


ID: B3-Ch12b-Away
TEXT:

Trading blows with a stillwater in a straight duel is suicide. I need another angle.

I bank hard on my air currents, diving toward the tree line where Daren holds the perimeter. Before I cover ten yards, Eiden displaces directly into my path, shaking his head.

"Fleeing the field, Barry?" Eiden sighs. "How profoundly disappointing."

I snap a reflex lightning bolt at his jaw, but he vanishes before the arc grounds.

I pivot mid-air, spraying a curtain of fire behind me to catch an invisible pursuit, but the flames meet empty air.

A hand clamps down onto the crown of my head from above. Concussive force detonates inward, shattering bone and ending thought in a heartbeat.

choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves)


ID: B3-Ch12b-Overconfident
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b2_ch9_animals != 2)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b2_ch9_animals == 2)
#if(v_b2_ch9_animals != 2) {
Eiden expects an evasive dive. Charging directly into the barrel of his spell will catch him off guard, stalling his cast long enough to sink the blade into his chest. A bold gamble.

I lean into my air currents, rocketing straight down the axis of his aim with the dagger locked in both fists.

Eiden's beam fires without hesitation. The torrent of white flame swallows me whole, incinerating flesh and bone to cinder in less than a second.

}
#if(v_b2_ch9_animals == 2) {
Eiden expects an evasive dive. Charging directly into the barrel of his spell will catch him off guard, stalling his cast long enough to sink the blade into his chest. A bold gamble.

I lean into my air currents, rocketing straight down the axis of his aim with the dagger locked in both fists.

The white flame erupts from his palm, engulfing me in blinding thermal fury—yet the heat simply parts around my skin, harmless as morning mist. I burst through the firestorm like an iron bolt, plunging the steel blade deep into his chest. The metal pierces through his passive barriers as if cutting silk.

"What?!" Eiden gasps, blood spilling over the collar of his tunic. "How did you... where did you obtain that talisman?!"

The wooden band on my left wrist pulses with brilliant amber luminescence, shielding my charge. The wolf's ancient ward held true.

Eiden teleports down to the cobblestones, clutching his chest as green healing light knits the puncture wound. My dagger remains in my grip as I descend.

Before the wound fully seals, Illuna snaps a dense sphere of swirling water over Eiden's head. The sudden immersion catches him mid-breath; he stumbles across the pavement, gasping and coughing as he tries to shake the watery cage. The spell holds fast.

Kate raises her scepter from the roadside, frost gathering at the tip.

"Kate, hold!" I shout, and she drops her aim on command.

He is wounded and disoriented, but his raw power can still deflect the freeze beam if he spots the cast. We need one final disruption to break his concentration.

Daren hurls his sword in a screaming spin toward Eiden's flank. Eiden raises a rock pillar from the road to divert the blade, then wraps himself in a roaring whirlwind. The gale scatters Illuna's water sphere into mist and throws Daren's blade off course.

Eiden cancels the vortex and collapses onto one knee, pressing a hand to his forehead as vertigo takes hold.

The opening is here.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b2_ch9_animals != 2)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_b2_ch9_animals != 2)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_b2_ch9_animals != 2)
