"If you say so!" Hadrik banks hard on his wings. "Make it count!"

"Admirable confidence, Barry," Eiden drifts forward. "Have we reached the finale?"

"Watch this," I say, striking the primary rune on my device three times in rapid succession.

"Adjusting your stats in the middle of a duel?" Eiden smiles, unimpressed. "You must know that no matter what you allocate, it won't—"

The aura siphon bites. Eiden's eyes snap wide as his mana bleeds into my conduits, and he lashes out with an instant fire blast.

